      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Thoracoscopy-talc led to the diagnosis of epithelial pleural mesothelioma in a 58-year-old man who presented with pleurisy. The course was rapidly unfavorable despite systemic chemotherapy. Dorsal pain revealed invasion of the spine and spinal canal leading to cord compression three months after the diagnosis of mesothelioma."},
